{title: Let the Day Perish}
{subtitle: Job 3:1–11; 30:16–23}
{key: Cm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Cm] | [Cm] | [Cm] | [Cm] |
| [Cm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Let the day perish [Bb]on which I was [Cm]born
And the night that [Bb]said, a boy is [Ab]conceived
Let that day [Bb]be darkness
[Ab]Let no light shine [Bb]upon it
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Cm]Why did I not die at [Bb]birth
[Cm]Why did I not breathe my [Bb]last
Why [Ab]is light given to the one in [Bb]misery
Why [Cm]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Now my life is [Bb]poured out within me
[Cm]Days of affliction have [Bb]taken hold of me
[Ab]Night pierces my [Bb]bones
[Ab]The pains that gnaw me never [Bb]rest
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Cm]I cry out to you, [Bb]and you do not answer
[Cm]I stand before you, and you [Bb]only look at me
You lift me [Ab]up to the [Bb]wind
You melt me away [Ab]in the roar of the storm
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Why [Bb]did I [Cm]not die at birth
Why did I not [Bb]breathe [Cm]my last
Why is light given to the [Bb]one in mi[Ab]sery
Why
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
I have become like [Bb]dust and ashes
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Cm] | [Cm] | [Abmaj7] | [Bb] | ×3
| [Cm] | [Cm] |
